class:: CoupledLogisticMap
summary:: Two symmetrically coupled trigger-driven logistic maps
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Maps
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/CoupledMapLattice, Classes/CircleMap

description::

Computes each logistic image code::f(x) = r*x*(1-x)::, then mixes the two images symmetrically by code::coupling::. It follows the coupled-map literature and does not force coordinates back into the conventional logistic interval.

The outputs are raw state coordinates. They are not normalized audio signals and may diverge for some parameters.

Like link::Classes/Stepper::, the pair updates on trigger edges and holds; unlike Stepper, each output depends on both nonlinear map images.

subsection:: State-space portrait

image::coupled-logistic-map-phase.png#The two coupled logistic states at the documented defaults. x is horizontal and y is vertical; diagonal structure shows synchronization between the maps.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: trig
Advance both maps on a rising edge.
argument:: rX
Logistic coefficient for x.
argument:: rY
Logistic coefficient for y.
argument:: coupling
Symmetric image-mixing amount; not clipped.
argument:: x0
Initial x coordinate.
argument:: y0
Initial y coordinate.
argument:: reset
Restore initial coordinates on a rising edge.
returns:: Two audio-rate outputs: x and y.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments and outputs.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ CoupledLogisticMap.ar(Impulse.ar(400))[0] * 0.1 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar(CoupledLogisticMap.kr(Impulse.kr(16))[1].linexp(0.05, 0.95, 80, 3000), 0, 0.08) }.play
)
::

subsection:: Real-time phase portrait

code::
(
SDPhaseView.open(
    "Coupled logistic map: x-y phase portrait",
    [0, 1], [0, 1],
    { CoupledLogisticMap.kr(Impulse.kr(90)) },
    { |state|
        Pan2.ar(
            SinOsc.ar(state[0].clip(0, 1).linexp(0, 1, 100, 1800), 0, 0.06),
            state[1].clip(0, 1).linlin(0, 1, -1, 1)
        )
    }
);
)
::

